<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
      MULTI-COMPANY ISOLATION.

      ir.model.access.csv says WHICH GROUPS may touch the model. It says
      nothing about WHICH RECORDS, and the addon shipped no ir.rule at all —
      so on a database with more than one company, a stock user in company A
      saw, and could approve, company B's transfer suggestions. The suggestion
      carries a donor, a recipient, quantities and a value: it is commercially
      sensitive between sibling companies, and approving one creates a document
      in a company the user does not belong to.

      This is not hypothetical here. The depot already contains a second
      company (CHIC1) alongside the 14 outlets.

      The domain is Odoo's standard multi-company shape. `company_id = False`
      is admitted deliberately: a record that belongs to no company must remain
      visible rather than becoming an orphan nobody can see or clean up.
      oasis_replace_queue now stamps company_id from the DONOR warehouse, so a
      row is owned by the company whose stock would actually move.

      oasis.sync needs no rule — it is an AbstractModel and stores no records.
    -->
    <record id="oasis_transfer_suggestion_company_rule" model="ir.rule">
        <field name="name">OASIS transfer suggestion: company isolation</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="model_oasis_transfer_suggestion"/>
        <field name="domain_force">
            ['|', ('company_id', '=', False), ('company_id', 'in', company_ids)]
        </field>
        <field name="global" eval="True"/>
    </record>
</odoo>
